WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.211 --> 00:00:02.794
(mellow music)

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.630
- [Narrator] On the
Italian island of Sardinia,

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.590
there's a delicacy that has been consumed

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:10.223
for thousands of years.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.693
It is known as the world's
most dangerous cheese.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.443
Yeah, you heard right.

00:00:21.046 --> 00:00:23.604
(mellow music)

00:00:23.604 --> 00:00:27.771
Meet Simone Ibba, a third
generation sheep farmer.

00:00:39.441 --> 00:00:42.300
- [Narrator] Casu marzu
literally means rotten cheese,

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.130
and it's not for the faint of heart,

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.000
because this cheese is infested

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.970
with thousands of live maggots.

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:51.880
And while that might seem
a bit off-putting at first,

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.970
it's the maggots that give the cheese

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.860
its distinctive texture and flavor.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:58.570
Here's how it works.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:01.030
First, a traditional
wheel of pecorino cheese

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:02.870
is made from sheep's milk.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.884
Then a special fly called a cheese fly

00:01:04.884 --> 00:01:07.013
is allowed to lay its eggs in it.

00:01:14.265 --> 00:01:16.410
- [Narrator] Over the
course of two to three months,

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:20.140
the maggots eat the cheese,
and then excrete it out again,

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.123
transforming it into the
soft and creamy casu marzu.

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:37.320
- [Narrator] Today, it's a
favorite for special occasions,

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.530
like weddings and birthday parties.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:42.107
But eating this cheese can be dangerous.

00:01:50.233 --> 00:01:53.300
- [Narrator] Even though cases
like this are extremely rare,

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.510
it's risky enough that the
cheese is illegal to sell.

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:59.703
But farmers like Simone continue
to make it for themselves.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.083
- [Narrator] And they
just can't get enough.

